From: luma-duo2 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] libhandy 0005: restore the truncated last hunk

The file ends mid-hunk. Its last hunk carries three lines of leading
context but only two of trailing context, and its header (-566,8 +567,19)
matches neither. GNU patch reads a hunk with less trailing than leading
context as anchored to the end of the file, so at --fuzz=0 (as the spec
applies it) the hunk is rejected even though every line matches the source.

Restore the missing third trailing context line,
  gtk_style_context_add_class (context, "unified");
which follows in hdy-window-mixin.c, and set the header to the hunk as it
now stands: 9 old lines, 21 new. It then applies at --fuzz=0 to libhandy
1.8.3 with Luma patches 0001-0004 applied.

diff --git a/patches/libhandy/0005-luma-one-title-row-per-window.patch b/patches/libhandy/0005-luma-one-title-row-per-window.patch
index 88e1004..1c00486 100644
--- a/patches/libhandy/0005-luma-one-title-row-per-window.patch
+++ b/patches/libhandy/0005-luma-one-title-row-per-window.patch
@@ -252,7 +252,7 @@ index 4bade07..66f36aa 100644
  #include "hdy-nothing-private.h"
  #include "hdy-window-mixin-private.h"
  
-@@ -566,8 +567,19 @@ hdy_window_mixin_new (GtkWindow      *window,
+@@ -566,9 +567,21 @@ hdy_window_mixin_new (GtkWindow      *window,
    GTK_CONTAINER_CLASS (self->klass)->add (GTK_CONTAINER (self->window),
                                            self->content);
  
@@ -274,3 +274,4 @@ index 4bade07..66f36aa 100644
 +  g_object_set_data (G_OBJECT (self->window), "luma-window-mixin-constructing", NULL);
  
    context = gtk_widget_get_style_context (GTK_WIDGET (self->window));
+   gtk_style_context_add_class (context, "unified");
